  "critical_scope": [
    "TwoStep ranks (b+2,a') -> (b,a'), explicitly a'<b and q>=1; p1+1=p and q1=q. Characters alpha,beta are unitary, so |z|=r^((a'-b)/2)<1.",
    "TwoStep conclusion Pure applies to every FinK k and every lower Sig1 f1 satisfying IsLow. FinK only imposes the source Cartan commutation condition at infinity, not compactness at all finite places.",
    "ConvCont: probability measure on X; an arbitrary left Haar measure on G. Bumps are nonnegative real continuous compactly supported, eta(1)!=0; no integral-one requirement.",
    "The staged rational unipotent quotient averages have mass one. Final Ctx.int_zero rescales the normalized zero mean to any source Haar/domain by its finite positive quotient volume.",
    "NonZeroAn keeps separate q-induction for p=0 and p-induction for q=0. Adapted polynomial test vanishing is transported through SchToPol and PolSch; small-side ToSo is retained.",
    "Original Geo.IsGood additionally has even a+a', a'<a, character-weight gap, natural (a-a')/2>2(p+q)+1, and a'>2(p+q)+1. These hypotheses are carried by original triples; the replacements do not weaken them.",
    "Line-cusp replacement retains KeyTwo and KeyThree. Their LocTwo/LocThree/VacBar/Places producers remain separate translation obligations."
  ]
}